<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Karbala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/680">680 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Karbala · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-fitna">Second Fitna</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Karbala was fought in 680 CE in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> between the forces of the Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazid-i">Yazid I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husayn-ibn-ali">Husayn ibn Ali</a>, grandson of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a>. Husayn and most of his small band were killed. The event became central to Shia identity and a lasting source of opposition to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-karbala.jpg" alt="Battle of Karbala" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Persian Painter Abbas Al-Musavi. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brooklyn_Museum_-_Battle_of_Karbala_-_Abbas_Al-Musavi_-_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
